# Realistic Oncology Cohort Validation Dataset

Generate a biologically realistic multi-omics oncology cohort in `data/realistic_cohort/`, then run the full OmicsFlow pipeline and produce a comprehensive PASS/FAIL validation report.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Generation Script

#### [NEW] [generate_realistic_cohort.R](file:///h:/omicsflow_test/generate_realistic_cohort.R)

A single R script that generates all data files into `data/realistic_cohort/`. **Does NOT touch `data/synthetic_cohort/`.**

**Patient Design (N=180):**
- **Subtype A — "Proliferative"** (60 patients): TP53-mutant, MYC-amplified, hypomethylated, high cell-cycle gene expression, worst prognosis (median OS ~400 days, 75% event rate)
- **Subtype B — "Mesenchymal"** (60 patients): COL1A1/FN1 ECM signature, intermediate methylation, moderate CNV burden, intermediate prognosis (median OS ~900 days, 55% event rate)
- **Subtype C — "Immune-enriched"** (60 patients): CD8A/PDCD1 immune markers, hypermethylated promoters, low CNV, best prognosis (median OS ~1600 days, 35% event rate)

**Biological Signal Architecture:**

| Data Layer | Subtype Signal | Survival Signal | Technical Noise |
|---|---|---|---|
| **RNA** (2000 genes × 180 samples) | 50 marker genes per subtype with shifted means | Top 20 genes correlated with OS via Cox coefficients | Batch shift (3 batches), center effect (2 centers) |
| **Methylation** (5000 probes × 180 samples) | Subtype-specific hyper/hypomethylation blocks | 30 probes with survival-correlated beta shifts | Batch-level beta offset |
| **CNV** (segments per patient) | Amplification/deletion hotspots per subtype | Gain in chr8q (MYC) associated with poor OS | Random background segments |
| **SNV** (MAF-like per patient) | Subtype-enriched driver mutations (TP53, KRAS, etc.) | TP53 mutation → worse survival | Varying TMB across subtypes |

**Survival Model:**
- Weibull distributions per subtype with distinct shape/scale
- Censoring via uniform administrative censoring (study end = 2500 days)
- Cox-linked molecular features: a weighted combination of ~10 gene expression features modulates individual hazard
- Target: 50-60% overall event rate, clinically realistic distributions

**Technical Effects:**
- 3 batches (B1, B2, B3) with additive shifts in RNA/meth
- 2 centers (Center_Alpha, Center_Beta) — confounded with batch (B1+B2 → Alpha, B3 → Beta)
- Batch effects are moderate (~10-20% of biological variance)

**Output Files:**
| File | Format | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `sample_metadata.csv` | CSV | sample_id, patient_id, sample_class, batch, center, subtype |
| `custom_clinical.tsv` | TSV | patient, OS_time, OS_event, age, sex, subtype, stage |
| `clinical_map.json` | JSON | Column mapping for clinical abstraction layer |
| `rna.rds` | RDS | Integer count matrix (2000 genes × 180 samples) with ENSEMBL rownames |
| `meth.rds` | RDS | Beta-value matrix (5000 cg-probes × 180 samples) |
| `cnv.rds` | RDS | Segment data.frame (Sample, Chromosome, Start, End, Segment_Mean, Num_Probes) |
| `snv.rds` | RDS | MAF-like data.frame (Tumor_Sample_Barcode, Hugo_Symbol, etc.) |

